url: 'https://www.seadatanet.org/Software/NEMO'
abstract: >-
  NEMO is a SeaDataNet software tool written in Java and
  designed to support marine data centres in the harmonisation
  and conversion of heterogeneous marine data files into
  SeaDataNet standard exchange formats.

  As part of the SeaDataNet CDI data discovery and access
  services, NEMO facilitates the preparation and integration
  of marine datasets into SeaDataNet workflows by converting
  heterogeneous ASCII formats into:

  - SeaDataNet ODV format
  - SeaDataNet MedAtlas ASCII format
  - SeaDataNet NetCDF (CF) format

  NEMO supports marine time series, profiles and trajectory
  observations.

  The software relies on SeaDataNet Common Vocabularies and
  the EDMO directory, which can be synchronised through
  dedicated online web services.

  NEMO contributes to the interoperability, harmonisation
  and FAIRification of marine observation data within the
  SeaDataNet infrastructure.
